{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1922","published":"2026-04-17T11:10:56Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:55.291546291Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-34982"],"summary":"vim security update","details":"Vim is an advanced text editor that seeks to provide the power of the de-facto Unix editor &amp;apos;Vi&amp;apos;, with a more complete feature set. Vim is a highly configurable text editor built to enable efficient text editing. It is an improved version of the vi editor distributed with most UNIX systems.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nVim is an open source, command line text editor. Prior to version 9.2.0276, a modeline sandbox bypass in Vim allows arbitrary OS command execution when a user opens a crafted file. The `complete`, `guitabtooltip` and `printheader` options are missing the `P_MLE` flag, allowing a modeline to be executed. Additionally, the `mapset()` function lacks a `check_secure()` call, allowing it to be abused from sandboxed expressions. Commit 9.2.0276 fixes the issue.(CVE-2026-34982)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"vim","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/vim&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["vim-X11-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","vim-common-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","vim-debuginfo-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","vim-debugsource-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","vim-enhanced-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","vim-minimal-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["vim-filesystem-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.noarch.rpm"],"src":["vim-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["vim-X11-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","vim-common-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","vim-debuginfo-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","vim-debugsource-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","vim-enhanced-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","vim-minimal-9.0.2092-29.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"sourc